course: dictionary
lesson: 4
title: Abandon: leaving behind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Abandon is a verb, and it means to leave something and not come back. «The family had to abandon their house after the flood.» The clue is that they had to leave because of danger, so abandon means leave for good.
explain: Abandon can also mean to stop something before it ends. «The match was abandoned because of rain.» Nobody left the pitch forever; the game just stopped early. Ask yourself: is a thing being left, or is a plan being stopped?
explain: The phrase «with abandon» is different. «She danced with abandon» means she danced in a wild, free way, without worrying what anyone thought. Here abandon is a noun, and the words around it give you the clue.
fact: Abandon is a verb: abandon, abandons, abandoned, abandoning.
fact: To abandon something means to leave it, and not come back to it.
fact: «Abandon ship!» means leave the ship, because it is in danger.
fact: «Abandoned» means left behind, often by someone who should have looked after it, such as a pet.
fact: Abandoning a pet is cruel and against the law. Animal shelters care for abandoned animals and find them new homes.
exercise: «The match was abandoned because of rain.» What does abandoned mean here? | *Stopped before the end | Watched on television | Played in the rain with no breaks | Started early, before the crowd arrived
exercise: «Abandon ship!» the captain shouted. What does he tell the crew to do? | Stay on board and wait | *Leave the ship because it is in danger | Clean the deck before lunch | Sail faster to the next island
exercise: «Nobody should abandon a pet.» What does abandon mean here? | *Leave it and never come back | Take it for a long walk | Give it a bath | Feed it every day
test: «She danced with abandon across the stage.» What does with abandon mean? | Sadly, with tears | *Wild and free, without worrying | Slowly and carefully | Badly, with lots of mistakes
test: The shelter found new homes for the abandoned dogs. What does abandoned mean? | Lost in the park for one day | Being trained for a dog show | Sleeping in a warm bed | *Left behind by their owners
exam: «They had to abandon their plan to camp because of the storm.» What does abandon mean here? | *Stop the plan before it ends | Plan it again with more people | Make the plan bigger | Ask someone else to do it
